Exploratory Testing 


Example 1

Date/Time: 10 June 2026, 11: 30pm
Tester: Prashant jadhav
Feature/Area: Multi-tab browsing – scientific reference (Wikispecies) 
Environment: Windows 11, Edge v149.0.4022.52

Charter (Focus):
Explore usability and accuracy when switching between a scientific taxonomy page (Purnella albifrons) and a general search tab.

Test Ideas & Scenarios Tried:

1) Opened Wikispecies page for Purnella albifrons and checked taxonomy details.
2) Switched to Bing search tab with “Wikipedia – Search” results.
3) Compared navigation speed between the two tabs.
4) Zoomed in/out on Wikispecies page to test layout stability.
5) Tried opening external links from Wikispecies page in new tabs.

Observations
Wikispecies page loads quickly, but taxonomy tables overlap slightly at 125% zoom.
Switching between tabs is smooth, though occasional flicker occurs when moving from Bing search back to Wikispecies.
External links open correctly but lack clear indication they lead outside the Wikispecies domain.
Search tab remains responsive, but results page refreshes unexpectedly after prolonged idle time.

Issues Found
Bug #001: Layout overlap at zoom 120% on Wikispecies taxonomy tables.
Bug #002: Tab flicker when switching from Bing search to Wikispecies.
Bug #003: External link usability issue (no indicator for external navigation).
Bug #004: Bing search tab refreshes unexpectedly after idle.
